# Tessera stdlib: how a crash stops a program without an operating system
#
# The Crash service reports a crash, then stops the program (Crash.te). With an operating system it exits with status
# 82. Without one the core stops in the way its architecture has (Unhosted's stop_core).

module System

import Unhosted

### Stops the program after a crash: the core stops (stop_core).
@target(os: "none")
@noreturn
common routine Crash.stop() -> None
    stop_core()
